WEBVTT

00:05.255 --> 00:06.881
[Sofia] I don't know
how to trust you.

00:08.466 --> 00:10.010
[Oz] How about
I keep showing you how?

00:10.010 --> 00:12.929
[tires screeching]

00:12.929 --> 00:14.556
[man] Don't move.
Don't fucking move.

00:14.556 --> 00:16.016
[Nadia speaks Farsi]

00:17.434 --> 00:20.437
[Taj] Down. On your knees.
I said on your fucking knees!

00:20.437 --> 00:22.814
Watch your goddamn mouth!
I ain't some kinda--

00:25.442 --> 00:27.777
[Oz grunting]

00:27.777 --> 00:30.697
The disrespect
you have shown our family...

00:31.489 --> 00:33.408
I know about the new drug.

00:33.950 --> 00:36.661
Your lab, it's ours now.

00:36.786 --> 00:38.955
Listen, it don't have
to go down this way.

00:38.955 --> 00:40.623
You think we'd just sit by,

00:40.623 --> 00:44.044
and watch you make
excuse after excuse,

00:44.044 --> 00:45.420
and do nothing?

00:45.420 --> 00:46.880
What the fuck
is she talking about?

00:47.005 --> 00:49.341
The second you walked
into Blackgate,

00:49.466 --> 00:52.802
I knew you were a swindler
and a cheat.

00:52.802 --> 00:54.262
What the fuck
is she talking about?

00:54.262 --> 00:55.680
Shut your goddamn mouth.

00:55.805 --> 00:58.808
Oh, I thought for a moment
you two were...

00:58.808 --> 01:00.852
that perhaps you asked him to...

01:00.977 --> 01:02.020
Asked him to what?

01:02.562 --> 01:03.938
[Nadia] Kill your brother...

01:04.731 --> 01:06.066
to take his place.

01:07.025 --> 01:09.110
But I'm wrong, aren't I?

01:09.903 --> 01:12.030
You didn't know.

01:12.155 --> 01:14.366
[dramatic music playing]

01:16.826 --> 01:17.911
You...

01:18.036 --> 01:19.537
Nadia, you gotta listen to me.

01:20.205 --> 01:21.623
I never cheated your family.

01:21.623 --> 01:23.541
Jesus! Come on!

01:24.084 --> 01:25.960
I needed Sofia
to get the new drug.

01:25.960 --> 01:27.545
All right? For us.

01:27.671 --> 01:30.090
It's yours. It's fucking yours!
I was gonna bring it to you.

01:30.090 --> 01:31.675
I swear to God.
You gotta trust me.

01:31.675 --> 01:33.051
I'm on your side.

01:33.176 --> 01:36.554
- [voice fades out]
- [dramatic music intensifies]

01:36.680 --> 01:38.098
[vehicle approaching rapidly]

01:39.599 --> 01:40.433
[Sofia grunts]

01:40.558 --> 01:41.476
[Oz grunts]

01:41.476 --> 01:42.936
[car alarm blaring]

01:43.061 --> 01:43.895
[gunshot]

01:46.189 --> 01:47.065
[Oz] Let's go!

01:48.024 --> 01:49.401
[dramatic music continues]

01:53.071 --> 01:54.823
[inaudible]

01:54.823 --> 01:56.741
- [tires screeching]
- [Nadia] Get in!

01:58.118 --> 01:59.077
[grunts]

01:59.577 --> 02:01.871
[panting]

02:01.871 --> 02:03.748
[engine revving]

02:03.873 --> 02:05.834
- [line rings]
- [Julian] Sofia?

02:05.834 --> 02:06.960
Julian.

02:07.419 --> 02:09.754
I need... I need help.

02:09.754 --> 02:10.964
[Julian] Where are you?

02:10.964 --> 02:15.176
[panting] It was... It...

02:15.176 --> 02:17.512
It was... Oz.

02:17.512 --> 02:18.680
[Julian] Sofia?

02:20.682 --> 02:21.641
Sofia?

02:23.643 --> 02:24.519
Sofia?!

02:25.103 --> 02:26.146
[music fades out]

02:26.980 --> 02:28.982
[woman] On behalf
of the Lucy House,

02:29.107 --> 02:32.277
it is my pleasure
to welcome the chairwoman

02:32.402 --> 02:35.530
of the Isabella Falcone
Foundation,

02:35.530 --> 02:37.615
Sofia Falcone.

02:37.741 --> 02:38.783
[applause]

02:51.087 --> 02:51.963
[applause stops]

02:52.589 --> 02:54.007
[Sofia exhales]

02:54.758 --> 02:58.219
I've never been one
for speeches, but, um...

03:00.055 --> 03:04.476
my mother, Isabella Falcone,

03:04.601 --> 03:07.812
struggled with depression
for years.

03:08.938 --> 03:11.232
She never got the help
that she needed,

03:11.232 --> 03:13.818
and when I was nine,

03:14.944 --> 03:16.654
she took her own life.

03:18.198 --> 03:20.617
That's why my father and I
started this foundation.

03:20.617 --> 03:23.912
We wanted to support charities
like this one

03:23.912 --> 03:28.249
that provide women and girls
with life-saving services.

03:28.833 --> 03:30.293
[applause]

03:31.461 --> 03:34.756
I'm so busy with our gala
and golf tournament next month.

03:34.756 --> 03:36.383
- Great speech.
- Thank you. Thank you.

03:36.383 --> 03:38.343
Sofia, you will be there,
won't you? It is so fun.

03:38.468 --> 03:39.678
Yes. I'm so sorry.
I have to run.

03:39.803 --> 03:41.054
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Mrs. Hill.

03:41.054 --> 03:42.847
You need a cigarette,
take the edge off?

03:42.972 --> 03:44.516
This is the third luncheon
this week.

03:44.641 --> 03:46.267
A lobotomy
couldn't take the edge off.

03:46.267 --> 03:48.311
I'm sure
your father appreciates it.

03:48.311 --> 03:50.063
But yeah, even when
you're helping people,

03:50.188 --> 03:51.856
you still gotta eat shit.
[laughs]

03:51.981 --> 03:53.525
It's better
than some jobs, though.

03:54.526 --> 03:56.486
Yeah, like what?
Driving me around?

03:56.486 --> 03:58.571
Nah, that ain't...
You know what I mean.

03:58.571 --> 03:59.989
Oz, I'm messing with you.

03:59.989 --> 04:01.700
It's a shitty job, I know.

04:01.825 --> 04:03.284
You deserve better.

04:03.827 --> 04:05.912
I mean, we both do,
but... you have a dick,

04:06.037 --> 04:08.123
so at least you're eligible
for a promotion.

04:08.123 --> 04:09.749
- [lighter opens]
- [laughs]

04:09.749 --> 04:10.709
[lighter clicks]

04:11.751 --> 04:13.044
[Oz] I'll get the car.

04:13.503 --> 04:14.754
- You did good.
- Thank you.

04:14.754 --> 04:15.922
Ms. Falcone.

04:16.673 --> 04:18.883
I know you're on your way out,
but do you have a minute?

04:20.844 --> 04:22.220
[blows] Sorry. Of course, yes.

04:22.345 --> 04:23.346
- I'm Summer Gleeson.
- Hi.

04:23.722 --> 04:25.306
Been following your work
with the Foundation.

04:25.306 --> 04:26.933
- It's impressive.
- Thank you.

04:26.933 --> 04:29.561
But if you don't mind me saying,
I think you could be doing more.

04:29.686 --> 04:30.812
I don't know if you're aware,

04:30.812 --> 04:33.148
but a young woman
named Yolanda Jones

04:33.148 --> 04:34.691
committed suicide last week.

04:34.691 --> 04:37.235
There's actually been
a number of women like Ms. Jones

04:37.360 --> 04:39.738
over the last decade,
and they all died the same way,

04:40.530 --> 04:41.406
by hanging.

04:42.032 --> 04:43.491
Which...
that's how your mother died

04:43.491 --> 04:45.076
if I'm not mistaken.

04:46.119 --> 04:47.704
- Um...
- I'm sorry. I don't mean to--

04:47.704 --> 04:49.622
You said there was something
I could do to help.

04:50.248 --> 04:52.375
Yolanda Jones worked
at the Iceberg Lounge.

04:52.375 --> 04:54.711
In fact, most of these women
worked for businesses

04:54.711 --> 04:56.087
owned by your father.

04:57.130 --> 04:59.424
What organization
did you say you were with?

04:59.549 --> 05:00.675
[tense music playing]

05:02.761 --> 05:03.845
I don't talk to press.

05:04.304 --> 05:06.014
- Sofia, please.
- I don't talk to press.

05:06.014 --> 05:08.767
Hey, hey! Back off, lady.
She don't wanna talk to you.

05:09.726 --> 05:11.353
[Summer]
More women could get hurt.

05:13.813 --> 05:15.023
You could help them.

05:16.441 --> 05:17.442
[car door closes]

05:19.944 --> 05:21.946
[music intensifies]

05:24.741 --> 05:25.825
You okay, Sofia?

05:28.411 --> 05:30.413
[young Sofia]
Ready or not, here I come!

05:30.413 --> 05:32.540
Alberto, I know you're in here.

05:35.710 --> 05:37.837
Alberto, where are you?

05:39.631 --> 05:40.799
[rope creaking]

05:52.686 --> 05:53.561
Mom?

06:01.528 --> 06:03.321
[music crescendos, ends]

06:03.446 --> 06:05.323
[Carmine] Sofia, how was
your luncheon?

06:06.700 --> 06:07.617
Good.

06:07.617 --> 06:09.744
[classical music playing]

06:12.330 --> 06:13.665
Ruth sends her regards.

06:14.207 --> 06:15.500
- Which one's Ruth?
- [texting]

06:16.001 --> 06:17.502
The wife of Congressman Hill...

06:19.462 --> 06:22.215
who's finally taking my calls,
thanks to your sister.

06:22.716 --> 06:24.551
- [texting]
- [phone whooshes]

06:24.676 --> 06:26.219
[chuckles, sniffs]

06:26.845 --> 06:29.222
[inhales] Right, right. Hill.

06:32.142 --> 06:34.602
I asked you to look into
his financial holdings.

06:34.602 --> 06:35.562
Uh...

06:36.312 --> 06:37.355
I'm working on it.

06:37.814 --> 06:38.982
I've been busy,

06:38.982 --> 06:41.192
but tomorrow, I promise.

06:42.360 --> 06:44.529
Why are you such a fool
when your sister's so reliable?

06:44.654 --> 06:46.114
I know, Pop.

06:46.114 --> 06:47.532
I get it. I'm sorry.

06:48.825 --> 06:49.701
[phone dings]

06:51.161 --> 06:52.162
Shit!

06:52.162 --> 06:54.289
I, uh... I gotta go.

07:04.257 --> 07:05.633
[knife clatters loudly]

07:05.633 --> 07:07.594
[sighs] I don't know
what to do with him.

07:09.512 --> 07:10.472
The drinking...

07:11.389 --> 07:12.307
the partying.

07:13.850 --> 07:16.061
I can't have your brother
embarrassing me next weekend,

07:16.186 --> 07:17.520
not with the Family flying in.

07:17.520 --> 07:19.981
I'm gonna watch him.
I'll make sure that he behaves.

07:21.107 --> 07:22.233
Thank you, beautiful.

07:25.904 --> 07:27.447
You know,
he's not like you and me.

07:29.366 --> 07:30.241
He's soft.

07:37.415 --> 07:40.085
I've been thinking recently
about the future...

07:41.378 --> 07:43.254
about our Family's future.

07:43.963 --> 07:45.799
Maybe it's time
to break with tradition.

07:46.883 --> 07:48.009
When the time comes,

07:49.094 --> 07:50.470
I want you to take my place.

07:53.431 --> 07:54.974
I want you to run this Family...

07:56.393 --> 07:58.144
if that's something
that would interest you.

07:58.144 --> 07:59.771
[chuckling] Yeah.

08:00.480 --> 08:01.481
Yeah, of course.

08:02.148 --> 08:04.651
I w-I would be... honored.

08:06.778 --> 08:07.904
But the rest of the Family--

08:07.904 --> 08:10.115
They know you're mine.
They'll do as I say.

08:15.704 --> 08:16.788
What? What is it?

08:18.790 --> 08:19.666
Tell me.

08:21.960 --> 08:22.836
Oh, it's nothing.

08:29.342 --> 08:30.260
I don't know.

08:32.178 --> 08:33.680
Maybe it's because
of the Foundation,

08:33.680 --> 08:37.976
but I've just been... [inhales]
...thinking a lot about Mom.

08:40.395 --> 08:41.396
Uh-huh.

08:49.988 --> 08:52.157
I know I was so young, but I...

08:53.700 --> 08:54.659
It's just...

08:55.326 --> 08:58.413
I don't remember her being sick

08:59.122 --> 09:00.331
or depressed.

09:01.166 --> 09:02.834
She was good at hiding it.

09:05.503 --> 09:08.089
Look, I miss her too, baby,
every day.

09:08.548 --> 09:12.344
Did she ever see anyone
before...

09:12.802 --> 09:15.347
Like a therapist
or a psychiatrist?

09:18.600 --> 09:20.185
Your mother was a proud woman...

09:21.686 --> 09:22.729
stubborn.

09:24.689 --> 09:26.191
She refused my help,

09:26.733 --> 09:28.902
as much as I tried, and...

09:29.903 --> 09:31.237
God knows I tried.

09:31.821 --> 09:33.114
Of course, yeah.

09:36.368 --> 09:38.203
- I just--
- Sofia.

09:40.872 --> 09:42.207
Why would you do this now?

09:44.334 --> 09:46.044
Picking away at old wounds...

09:46.503 --> 09:48.171
You know how it upsets me.

09:48.171 --> 09:50.882
I'm sorry. I didn't...
I-I-I didn't mean to.

09:59.224 --> 10:01.601
You still haven't told me
what you want for your birthday.

10:05.105 --> 10:05.980
[chuckles]

10:07.524 --> 10:09.484
I'm sure I'll love it,
whatever you get me.

10:12.737 --> 10:14.989
[downbeat hip-hop music playing]

10:14.989 --> 10:16.658
[music continues]

10:20.578 --> 10:21.579
[Alberto] Don't worry.

10:24.082 --> 10:25.542
Pop's gonna lose his shit
over it.

10:25.542 --> 10:26.710
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

10:26.710 --> 10:28.336
How do you know?

10:28.336 --> 10:30.338
'Cause it's old and expensive,
like his favorite child.

10:30.338 --> 10:31.506
[ice rattles]

10:31.506 --> 10:33.591
[tuts] Shit! [wipes pants]

10:33.717 --> 10:35.927
Your Penguin up there
is gonna have to clean this up.

10:36.052 --> 10:36.928
Don't call him that.

10:37.429 --> 10:39.556
- You'll take care of the card?
- [Sofia] Yeah.

10:40.265 --> 10:42.434
Wait. Wait, wait.
Can I ask you something?

10:43.435 --> 10:44.894
The girls at the 44 Below,

10:44.894 --> 10:49.691
h-has Dad ever had relationships
with them?

10:51.985 --> 10:54.487
Those girls aren't exactly
the relationship type.

10:55.613 --> 10:58.074
Since when do you care
about Pop's love life?

10:58.074 --> 10:59.451
It's been a long time since Mom,

10:59.576 --> 11:02.120
and he doesn't really talk to me
about it, and...

11:02.746 --> 11:04.914
I don't know. You get to see
a whole 'nother side of him.

11:04.914 --> 11:06.791
- What side? He's Pop.
- Yeah, I know.

11:06.916 --> 11:09.794
But you know what I mean.
It's very different with me.

11:11.296 --> 11:13.340
I just thought
you might have seen something.

11:14.591 --> 11:15.884
What are you asking?

11:15.884 --> 11:17.302
I guess I...

11:18.678 --> 11:20.221
Sometimes, I wonder if I...

11:21.639 --> 11:22.515
really...

11:23.975 --> 11:25.185
really know him.

11:25.810 --> 11:28.146
Like, with all the lies
that we had to tell growing up

11:28.271 --> 11:30.190
about what he does,
and there's...

11:30.190 --> 11:32.025
there's a lot
that we don't talk about.

11:33.485 --> 11:35.153
There is something, but...

11:37.947 --> 11:39.699
I can't. He'd fucking kill me.

11:42.035 --> 11:42.911
[Alberto sighs]

11:43.995 --> 11:45.372
Pop's...

11:45.497 --> 11:46.498
Mossad,

11:47.290 --> 11:49.292
and the girls at the club
are trained female assassins.

11:49.292 --> 11:51.086
- Shut up!
- [Alberto laughs]

11:51.086 --> 11:53.755
Listen, whatever
you're thinking, don't.

11:53.755 --> 11:56.675
What Pop does at work,
he does at work.

11:57.550 --> 12:01.179
I mean,
we got a good life, right?

12:07.394 --> 12:08.561
Where to, Sofia?

12:10.063 --> 12:11.189
[somber music playing]

12:13.525 --> 12:15.944
[train passing]

12:19.906 --> 12:21.032
[Summer] This is everything.

12:21.825 --> 12:23.159
Coroner reports are consistent.

12:23.159 --> 12:26.579
They all died from asphyxia.

12:26.705 --> 12:28.123
I'm not disputing that.

12:28.123 --> 12:29.708
What I find strange is,

12:29.833 --> 12:31.001
according to the police,

12:31.001 --> 12:34.587
official cause of death
is suicide by hanging.

12:35.839 --> 12:38.049
Do you see the impressions
around the neck?

12:38.550 --> 12:41.428
They're far more congruent
with manual strangulation.

12:41.553 --> 12:42.762
Like someone's hands?

12:43.346 --> 12:44.305
Exactly.

12:44.848 --> 12:46.599
Then there's
the defensive wounds.

12:46.599 --> 12:48.727
They were left off
the police reports.

12:49.436 --> 12:51.229
You can see these women,
they fought back.

12:51.354 --> 12:52.939
Biting, scratching... They--

12:53.064 --> 12:54.566
Why are you telling me this?

12:56.776 --> 12:59.112
I need access to the girls
working at the club.

12:59.696 --> 13:00.697
It's not exclusive.

13:00.697 --> 13:02.949
Not the Iceberg Lounge,
the 44 Below,

13:03.074 --> 13:05.326
where Yolanda Jones
actually worked.

13:06.286 --> 13:08.413
- If you wore a wire--
- To my father's club?

13:09.039 --> 13:10.123
Never gonna happen.

13:10.248 --> 13:12.334
Then just give me access
to employee records.

13:12.334 --> 13:13.668
Women who are new in town,

13:13.668 --> 13:16.338
who don't have
family or friends close by,

13:16.338 --> 13:17.964
the type whose death
or disappearance

13:18.089 --> 13:19.424
doesn't make the news.

13:20.091 --> 13:21.718
We need to protect these women.

13:21.843 --> 13:24.429
- [menacing music playing]
- [young Sofia] Mom?

13:26.765 --> 13:27.932
[rope creaking]

13:30.977 --> 13:33.271
Oh, no. No, no. Sofia.

13:35.106 --> 13:36.274
Don't look.

13:37.734 --> 13:38.651
Don't look.

13:39.986 --> 13:40.862
Dad.

13:44.574 --> 13:45.533
[Summer] Sofia?

13:47.285 --> 13:49.120
- Sofia, what is it?
- [inhales]

13:51.289 --> 13:52.457
This is all you have?

13:53.083 --> 13:54.125
That's it?

13:54.459 --> 13:58.046
Just, like, some old reports
and conspiracy theories?

13:58.046 --> 13:59.339
It's ridiculous.

14:00.256 --> 14:01.800
And it reeks

14:01.925 --> 14:04.636
of a junior reporter
desperate for a byline.

14:04.761 --> 14:05.720
Sofia, please, just--

14:05.720 --> 14:08.223
You don't know shit
about my father.

14:08.223 --> 14:10.475
He is a good man!

14:11.476 --> 14:13.645
And if you try publishing
any of this garbage,

14:13.770 --> 14:16.147
my family will destroy you.

14:16.981 --> 14:18.316
[inhales] Do you understand?

14:20.485 --> 14:21.528
[tense music playing]

14:31.287 --> 14:34.582
[breathing shakily]

14:34.582 --> 14:35.542
[car door closes]

14:37.293 --> 14:39.170
[Oz] That the same lady
from the luncheon?

14:40.630 --> 14:42.257
Look, Sofia,
meeting a reporter...

14:43.008 --> 14:44.884
people are gonna start
to get ideas.

14:45.010 --> 14:46.011
Your father might not like--

14:46.136 --> 14:47.012
Oz, stop!

14:48.972 --> 14:50.932
Stop talking.

14:50.932 --> 14:52.267
I don't need your advice.

14:52.267 --> 14:55.353
I don't care what you think.
No one does.

14:55.478 --> 14:56.980
You are my driver.
That is all you are.

14:56.980 --> 14:58.690
So stop talking and drive.

15:05.238 --> 15:06.531
[engine starts]

15:13.038 --> 15:14.497
[indistinct chatter
and laughter]

15:14.497 --> 15:15.707
[jazz music playing]

15:16.708 --> 15:17.751
[Carla] Sofia!

15:19.711 --> 15:20.920
Sofia.

15:20.920 --> 15:23.381
- Carla!
- Aw, Sofia! Thank God!

15:24.174 --> 15:26.593
Have you seen
bride number three?

15:26.593 --> 15:29.262
- [giggles derisively]
- Oh, my God.

15:29.387 --> 15:30.555
- It's a lot.
- It's a lot.

15:30.680 --> 15:32.974
[laughing] Yeah. Yeah.

15:32.974 --> 15:35.018
Luca says he met her
in Portugal.

15:35.143 --> 15:36.019
Okay.

15:36.895 --> 15:38.396
[Luca speaking indistinctly]

15:38.521 --> 15:39.898
Portugal.com.

15:40.023 --> 15:42.067
[laughing] Oh... Yeah.

15:42.609 --> 15:45.028
You must catch me up
on absolutely everything.

15:45.028 --> 15:46.863
- Oh my God, yeah. Absolutely.
- Everything.

15:46.863 --> 15:48.823
- First, a martini?
- Obviously.

15:48.823 --> 15:50.033
[both laugh]

15:50.033 --> 15:51.785
Sofia. Hey.

15:52.285 --> 15:53.953
Oz, what are you doing inside?

15:55.163 --> 15:57.165
- [grunts]
- Is that a new jacket?

15:57.165 --> 15:58.166
Yeah, yeah.

15:59.042 --> 16:00.835
- Looks good.
- Thank you.

16:00.835 --> 16:02.462
Uh, your father wants
to see you.

16:03.213 --> 16:04.255
He's in his office.

16:29.447 --> 16:31.616
Don't tell me you're sick
of the party already.

16:32.575 --> 16:35.120
Uncle Luca hasn't even told
his vasectomy story yet.

16:35.245 --> 16:37.205
Why didn't you tell me
you met with a reporter?

16:37.205 --> 16:41.292
You never, ever talk
to the press.

16:41.418 --> 16:42.377
[glass thuds on table]

16:42.836 --> 16:44.129
I thought you understood that.

16:44.713 --> 16:45.880
Did Oz tell you that?

16:47.549 --> 16:50.135
Oz doesn't know
what he's talking about.

16:50.260 --> 16:53.388
Some woman approached me,
but I told her to fuck off.

16:53.388 --> 16:54.305
That's it.

16:54.431 --> 16:55.598
Is that right?

16:56.266 --> 16:57.726
Mm-hmm. Yeah.

16:58.518 --> 16:59.477
Dad...

16:59.602 --> 17:01.062
[tense music playing]

17:01.062 --> 17:02.731
I spoke to Kenzie.

17:02.731 --> 17:06.151
Summer Gleeson has been working
with the police.

17:07.694 --> 17:09.571
There's an open investigation.

17:11.031 --> 17:12.657
They're looking into me
for murder.

17:14.659 --> 17:16.202
Murder, Sofia.

17:17.287 --> 17:18.997
Some hookers at the club.

17:21.332 --> 17:23.835
- Why didn't you come to me?
- I should have. You're right.

17:23.960 --> 17:27.005
But I knew it was bullshit,
and I didn't wanna worry you.

17:27.130 --> 17:28.006
Stop.

17:29.215 --> 17:31.009
Do you think I did these things?

17:32.052 --> 17:33.428
No, of course not.

17:33.428 --> 17:35.263
You were supposed
to be better than this.

17:36.181 --> 17:37.057
This...

17:38.016 --> 17:39.017
was meant for you.

17:41.144 --> 17:42.103
All of it.

17:43.063 --> 17:44.356
How could you do this to me?

17:44.856 --> 17:47.359
I-I didn't... I-I've never...

17:48.443 --> 17:50.028
I've never doubted you.

17:51.571 --> 17:52.447
I love you.

17:53.156 --> 17:55.575
And I know, I know
that there is an explanation.

17:56.284 --> 17:57.744
An explanation for what?

18:00.872 --> 18:01.873
[inhales shakily]

18:01.873 --> 18:04.459
You had scratches
on-on your hands

18:05.168 --> 18:06.544
the day Mom died.

18:09.422 --> 18:11.049
[Carmine breathes heavily]

18:11.174 --> 18:12.342
[menacing music plays]

18:12.342 --> 18:15.762
But I know-I know
they weren't from her.

18:15.887 --> 18:18.223
I know that. I-I, um...

18:19.349 --> 18:20.392
They were from...

18:22.185 --> 18:23.603
something else. I...

18:23.728 --> 18:25.313
I don't know what, but...

18:27.357 --> 18:29.067
S-s-something.

18:31.194 --> 18:33.238
[eerie, menacing music playing]

18:39.911 --> 18:40.995
Right?

18:47.377 --> 18:48.378
My...

18:49.754 --> 18:51.172
sweet Sofia.

18:53.550 --> 18:54.759
What has happened to you?

18:57.762 --> 18:59.180
You're clearly not yourself.

19:00.807 --> 19:04.102
You're confused, sick.

19:07.230 --> 19:09.149
I think you need to leave
before you make a scene.

19:12.444 --> 19:14.112
Dad, please, please--

19:14.112 --> 19:15.488
Oz will drive you home.

19:16.698 --> 19:17.574
Now.

19:19.451 --> 19:21.161
[door opens]

19:28.960 --> 19:30.670
Listen, I get that you're angry,
you know.

19:30.795 --> 19:32.172
But I was just doing my job,

19:32.839 --> 19:33.923
looking out for you.

19:33.923 --> 19:35.967
That's what
your father pays me for.

19:36.509 --> 19:38.261
These reporters,
they get in your head.

19:38.261 --> 19:40.013
- You can't trust 'em.
- Jesus, Oz, shut up!

19:40.138 --> 19:41.598
If you were really looking out
for me,

19:41.598 --> 19:44.309
you would've talked to me,
not him.

19:44.976 --> 19:47.228
[inhales] I trusted you.

19:49.981 --> 19:52.484
Congratulations.
You got what you wanted.

19:53.151 --> 19:54.486
My father sees you now.

19:55.278 --> 19:58.198
You and everyone you love
is on his radar.

19:58.198 --> 19:59.824
[siren approaching]

19:59.949 --> 20:02.535
Come on. What the fuck is this?

20:06.998 --> 20:07.957
[car shifts into park]

20:07.957 --> 20:09.084
- [siren chirps]
- [Oz sighs]

20:09.834 --> 20:10.835
[window lowering]

20:13.672 --> 20:15.590
Come on, Kenzie. You wanna kill
the circus lights?

20:15.590 --> 20:18.051
I'm taking Ms. Falcone home.
Father's orders.

20:20.136 --> 20:22.222
Ms. Falcone, step outside.

20:22.681 --> 20:24.933
- [Oz] What is this?
- Did my dad call you?

20:24.933 --> 20:26.476
[Kenzie] Step out of the car.

20:26.476 --> 20:28.937
Oh, my God. Are you kidding me?

20:29.938 --> 20:30.814
[Sofia sighs]

20:33.149 --> 20:34.192
[Kenzie] Sofia Falcone.

20:35.318 --> 20:36.820
- Get off me. Wait!
- You're under arrest

20:36.820 --> 20:38.488
for the murder
of Summer Gleeson.

20:38.488 --> 20:40.281
- The reporter?
- What?!

20:40.824 --> 20:42.701
Did you do this? For him?

20:42.826 --> 20:44.577
No. I got no idea
what the fuck is going on.

20:44.577 --> 20:46.496
- Kenzie, what the fuck?
- You're also being charged

20:46.496 --> 20:48.039
with the murder
of Yolanda Jones,

20:48.164 --> 20:49.582
Taylor Montgomery,
and Nancy Hoffman.

20:49.582 --> 20:51.876
- Get out of here with that!
- No, I didn't kill anyone!

20:52.002 --> 20:54.004
Oz, you gotta do something!

20:54.004 --> 20:55.714
Hey, let her go!

20:55.839 --> 20:57.882
Take my advice
and shut the fuck up, Penguin.

20:58.008 --> 20:59.009
Oz, call Alberto!

20:59.009 --> 21:01.636
[struggling] Stop! Call Alberto!

21:01.636 --> 21:04.931
- Get your fucking hands off--
- Tell him what's going on! Oz!

21:08.184 --> 21:09.060
[Sofia] The Hangman?

21:09.769 --> 21:11.438
That's what they're calling me?

21:11.438 --> 21:13.481
It's just tabloid bullshit.
It'll pass.

21:13.481 --> 21:15.692
Sofia, your father's claiming

21:15.692 --> 21:17.402
that you have a history
of mental illness.

21:17.527 --> 21:18.778
Well, that's ridiculous.

21:18.778 --> 21:20.321
[lawyer] The ADA met
with the judge,

21:20.321 --> 21:22.907
and the court has ordered
a psychological evaluation.

21:23.033 --> 21:24.325
Because my dad said so?

21:24.325 --> 21:25.744
[lawyer]
It's not just your father.

21:25.869 --> 21:28.747
A number of family members
have written affidavits

21:28.872 --> 21:30.165
suggesting the same.

21:30.165 --> 21:31.875
Your uncle Luca.

21:31.875 --> 21:34.336
Your cousins
Johnny and Carla Viti.

21:34.336 --> 21:36.880
They're using
my mother's suicide as a...

21:36.880 --> 21:38.465
[sighs heavily]

21:39.341 --> 21:41.718
I have a compulsion
for killing animals?

21:41.718 --> 21:43.636
Are you fucking serious?

21:44.095 --> 21:46.514
- Did you know about this?
- No. I swear.

21:49.392 --> 21:50.602
So, I, uh...

21:50.727 --> 21:52.771
I do an evaluation, and I, um...

21:52.896 --> 21:55.565
answer a few questions
to prove I'm sane, right?

21:55.565 --> 21:57.442
That's it, right? Then what?

21:57.567 --> 21:59.361
[lawyer] I'm afraid
it's not that simple.

21:59.361 --> 22:02.322
The judge agreed
to the ADA's request.

22:02.322 --> 22:04.866
You're being remanded
to Arkham State Hospital

22:04.866 --> 22:05.909
for observation.

22:05.909 --> 22:07.285
No.

22:07.577 --> 22:09.746
[laughs incredulously] No.
That doesn't make any sense.

22:09.746 --> 22:12.624
You'll be under their care
till the start of trial.

22:12.624 --> 22:13.917
When is that?

22:13.917 --> 22:15.335
[lawyer] Six months from now.

22:16.002 --> 22:17.337
- Oh, my God!
- [lawyer] I'm sorry.

22:17.462 --> 22:19.214
No. I'm not doing that.

22:20.256 --> 22:21.841
I am not doing that.

22:23.718 --> 22:26.429
Can't you stop this? You're my--
You're my fucking lawyer!

22:26.429 --> 22:27.472
[lawyer] I'm sorry.

22:29.099 --> 22:30.308
I'll give you two a minute.

22:32.018 --> 22:33.645
- [Alberto sighs]
- [door opens, closes]

22:33.770 --> 22:36.606
He is punishing me
for something he did.

22:36.606 --> 22:37.774
You don't know that.

22:37.774 --> 22:40.819
Alberto, wake up!
Are you kidding me?!

22:41.361 --> 22:42.821
He strangled those women,

22:42.946 --> 22:44.739
and then he strangled
that reporter

22:44.739 --> 22:46.908
and strung her up
to pin it on me.

22:46.908 --> 22:49.494
[breathing raggedly]
He did the same thing to Mom.

22:50.161 --> 22:51.996
It's true.
And I'm not gonna make it.

22:52.122 --> 22:54.499
I'm not gonna make it
in a place like that.

22:54.624 --> 22:56.334
[crying] I'm gonna die in there.

22:56.835 --> 22:59.504
I'm gonna die in there,
and he knows it. He knows it.

22:59.629 --> 23:01.214
- That's what he wants.
- Stop.

23:02.132 --> 23:03.633
It's only six months.

23:03.633 --> 23:05.677
- You can handle six months.
- [Sofia exhales]

23:05.802 --> 23:07.846
And then
you're gonna get a trial,

23:07.846 --> 23:09.097
and you're gonna get out.

23:09.097 --> 23:10.181
You are, God damn it.

23:10.306 --> 23:11.725
- I promise you.
- [lawyer] It's time.

23:13.810 --> 23:15.020
Wait. Right now?

23:15.562 --> 23:18.231
Listen, you're
a fucking Falcone.

23:18.356 --> 23:19.232
You can do this.

23:19.566 --> 23:21.526
- I know you can.
- No, no, no, no. Wait. Stop.

23:21.651 --> 23:22.944
Please, stop. Please.

23:22.944 --> 23:24.237
[Alberto] Sofia!

23:24.362 --> 23:26.489
- Please, please!
- [Alberto] It's gonna be okay.

23:26.489 --> 23:27.532
Alberto!

23:28.033 --> 23:29.367
[Alberto] Don't let him win.

23:30.243 --> 23:32.203
Please. Alberto!

23:32.328 --> 23:33.121
[door slams shut]

23:33.121 --> 23:35.707
[intense dramatic music playing]

23:45.258 --> 23:47.135
- [water spraying]
- [gasping]

23:58.104 --> 23:59.481
[scrubbing violently]

24:06.237 --> 24:07.113
[thud]

24:10.533 --> 24:11.910
[gasps]

24:14.621 --> 24:16.414
[handcuffs clicking]

24:16.956 --> 24:18.083
[neck collar clanking]

24:18.208 --> 24:20.794
[shackles rattling]

24:20.919 --> 24:21.836
[music ends abruptly]

24:21.836 --> 24:23.963
[man] Falcone, Sofia.

24:24.422 --> 24:26.758
I'm Dr. Ventris,
chief psychiatrist.

24:26.883 --> 24:29.469
I'll be overseeing your care
for the next six months.

24:29.594 --> 24:32.722
This is my associate,
Dr. Julian Rush.

24:32.722 --> 24:35.350
He'll be conducting
the psychological evaluation.

24:35.350 --> 24:36.559
While here, you'll be under

24:36.559 --> 24:38.728
court-ordered
mandatory isolation,

24:38.728 --> 24:40.772
which means no visitors,
no outside contact.

24:40.897 --> 24:41.898
Wait, what?

24:41.898 --> 24:43.274
It's important for us
to observe you

24:43.400 --> 24:44.693
without interference.

24:44.693 --> 24:46.653
No, no, no. Wait!
Wait a second. Wait a second!

24:46.653 --> 24:48.863
There's-there's been
a mistake here, okay?

24:48.863 --> 24:51.116
And I know--
Stop. Please, just...

24:51.241 --> 24:52.659
I know that people say that
all the time,

24:52.784 --> 24:54.077
but it is true, all right?

24:54.077 --> 24:57.080
I am innocent! Please!

24:57.080 --> 24:59.416
I realize this is
a difficult adjustment.

24:59.416 --> 25:02.127
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door clangs open]

25:02.252 --> 25:04.087
[somber music playing]

25:04.087 --> 25:05.672
[Sofia breathing heavily]

25:06.339 --> 25:07.215
Shall we?

25:08.466 --> 25:09.634
[door slams shut]

25:09.759 --> 25:11.302
[screams and unhinged laughter
in distance]

25:11.428 --> 25:13.304
[eerie, menacing music playing]

25:17.976 --> 25:19.060
[Julian] Follow me.

25:19.060 --> 25:21.146
[Sofia panting]

25:22.480 --> 25:24.107
[buzzer sounds]

25:24.107 --> 25:25.650
[screaming in distance]

25:40.123 --> 25:41.124
[music fades]

25:41.124 --> 25:42.500
[Julian] Get some rest.

25:45.503 --> 25:47.839
- [door slams, locks]
- [buzzer sounds]

25:49.299 --> 25:50.675
[somber music playing]

25:55.889 --> 25:56.890
[distant thud]

25:56.890 --> 26:00.018
[shouting and moaning
in distance]

26:00.143 --> 26:01.519
[eerie music playing]

26:03.813 --> 26:04.647
[crying]

26:04.647 --> 26:06.066
- [metal clangs]
- [Sofia gasps]

26:07.650 --> 26:08.735
[squeaky female voice] Hi.

26:10.362 --> 26:11.279
Hello.

26:12.530 --> 26:13.406
Up here.

26:14.532 --> 26:15.408
[sniffles]

26:19.704 --> 26:20.914
[exhales]

26:21.039 --> 26:22.749
- [guard] Lights out!
- [thudding]

26:24.334 --> 26:26.086
[squeaky voice]
You're the Hangman, aren't you?

26:26.211 --> 26:27.253
[breathing excitedly]

26:27.253 --> 26:30.131
I saw you on the TV.
[giggles shrilly]

26:31.758 --> 26:33.635
My name is Magpie.

26:34.094 --> 26:36.137
Like the bird. [giggles]

26:36.763 --> 26:38.014
Not "Margaret."

26:38.014 --> 26:40.016
My stepmom
used to call me "Margaret,"

26:40.016 --> 26:42.310
and I told her not to,
and she didn't listen.

26:43.019 --> 26:45.188
- [screaming in distance]
- [gasps]

26:45.855 --> 26:49.150
[Magpie] It's okay to be scared.
I was scared at first, too,

26:49.150 --> 26:52.946
but it's not so bad here.
You get used to the noises.

26:53.071 --> 26:54.364
I'm getting out in six months.

26:54.364 --> 26:55.824
[Magpie] Isn't that exciting?

26:55.824 --> 26:58.785
Ooh, I bet there'll be
lots of paparazzi at your trial.

26:58.785 --> 27:01.621
- No one even wrote about mine.
- [distant screaming continues]

27:01.621 --> 27:04.958
[Magpie] Is it fun being famous?
Oh, I bet it's fun.

27:06.126 --> 27:08.211
Hangman? Hangman?

27:08.211 --> 27:09.587
[screaming intensifies]

27:09.713 --> 27:13.174
[Magpie echoes in sing-song]
Hangman...

27:13.174 --> 27:14.926
[patients clamoring loudly]

27:17.053 --> 27:19.097
[patient]
Check out the new chick.

27:19.556 --> 27:21.641
[patients whistling]

27:21.766 --> 27:23.518
[patient taunting indistinctly]

27:24.728 --> 27:26.521
[patient] Hangman.

27:29.149 --> 27:30.734
[patient 2] Hey, pretty lady.

27:30.734 --> 27:31.901
[whistling]

27:33.486 --> 27:35.280
[patients whooping]

27:35.405 --> 27:36.281
[Magpie] Hangman.

27:37.073 --> 27:38.867
Hangman! It's me, Magpie.

27:38.867 --> 27:40.869
I saved you a seat. [giggles]

27:47.250 --> 27:49.794
Dr. V says it's important
that I make friends.

27:50.587 --> 27:52.797
Sometimes, I have a problem
with that.

27:53.840 --> 27:55.300
But I'm making progress.

27:57.927 --> 27:59.471
[gasps excitedly] Candy!

28:00.680 --> 28:01.556
Mmm.

28:01.556 --> 28:02.474
What is that?

28:03.183 --> 28:04.225
[sighs contentedly]

28:05.852 --> 28:06.978
[sighing happily]

28:07.645 --> 28:10.190
You only get it
when you're good.

28:10.648 --> 28:11.900
[giggles softly]

28:14.986 --> 28:16.571
[swallows heavily]

28:17.781 --> 28:20.158
[exhaling softly]

28:27.707 --> 28:28.833
[tense music playing]

28:30.210 --> 28:33.004
What is she--
Shouldn't she be chained?

28:33.630 --> 28:35.632
[laughing menacingly]

28:38.468 --> 28:40.053
[quietly] Hey. Hey.

28:40.178 --> 28:43.682
[inhales sharply] Wow!
Do you see that? The colors?

28:44.516 --> 28:46.101
It's all so shiny.

28:46.101 --> 28:49.354
Hey, she's not...
She-she-she's not chained.

28:52.941 --> 28:55.694
You killed those girls.

28:56.486 --> 28:59.698
Girls. Girls. Girls.

28:59.823 --> 29:02.742
[patients shouting indistinctly]

29:02.867 --> 29:04.202
I-I didn't kill anyone.

29:04.327 --> 29:05.620
- [gasps]
- [woman] You're lying.

29:06.162 --> 29:07.372
[Sofia gasping]

29:07.372 --> 29:11.167
She's lying!
Lying. Lying. Lying.

29:11.167 --> 29:12.085
[Sofia screams]

29:12.085 --> 29:14.087
[patients shouting]

29:16.423 --> 29:17.382
[screams]

29:18.091 --> 29:20.552
[yelling angrily]

29:20.677 --> 29:24.556
[woman] You killed them!
Say it! Say it! Say it!

29:28.226 --> 29:29.227
[music ends]

29:30.562 --> 29:31.479
[coughing]

29:32.897 --> 29:35.066
[gasping]

29:37.819 --> 29:38.695
[gasps]

29:40.530 --> 29:41.823
[exhales painfully]

29:41.823 --> 29:44.159
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door opens]

29:49.080 --> 29:50.832
- [door clanks shut]
- [buzzer sounds]

29:50.832 --> 29:52.292
[Julian] How are you feeling?

29:52.292 --> 29:55.670
I heard you had an incident
in the mess hall today.

29:56.379 --> 29:58.381
A woman beat the shit out of me

29:58.381 --> 30:00.258
while everyone stood around
and watched.

30:00.383 --> 30:03.303
So, yeah, I had an incident.
Yeah. [winces]

30:03.303 --> 30:04.846
I'm sorry that happened to you.

30:06.431 --> 30:09.309
Why was she unchained?

30:09.934 --> 30:11.061
I don't know.

30:11.936 --> 30:13.104
They're looking into it.

30:14.731 --> 30:16.775
Did someone release her?

30:16.900 --> 30:18.151
Is that what you believe?

30:18.610 --> 30:20.445
The attack in there
was coordinated?

30:23.573 --> 30:26.284
- I know what you're doing.
- What's that?

30:26.409 --> 30:29.287
You're twisting my words around
to make me sound paranoid.

30:29.871 --> 30:30.997
But you weren't there.

30:31.122 --> 30:33.458
Someone h-had
to have set her free.

30:37.837 --> 30:39.798
You've been in therapy before,
I see.

30:39.923 --> 30:41.841
With, uh, Dr. Shaw.

30:43.009 --> 30:44.135
After your mother died.

30:48.556 --> 30:51.643
The death of a parent
is a traumatic event,

30:51.768 --> 30:53.395
and it's not unusual

30:53.395 --> 30:56.648
to transfer that grief
into anger

30:57.482 --> 30:58.400
or even violence.

30:58.608 --> 31:02.320
It's not unusual
to just be sad, either.

31:02.779 --> 31:03.697
Right?

31:04.781 --> 31:06.157
I didn't kill those women.

31:07.450 --> 31:09.202
I would never do
anything like that.

31:11.329 --> 31:12.497
I am here

31:13.206 --> 31:18.211
because my father
wants to keep me quiet,

31:18.211 --> 31:20.130
and my family will do
whatever he says.

31:20.130 --> 31:21.840
So you're saying
that your father

31:22.716 --> 31:24.217
framed you for murder?

31:27.095 --> 31:28.346
You don't believe me.

31:29.055 --> 31:30.181
I didn't say that.

31:30.849 --> 31:32.225
I can tell.

31:35.311 --> 31:37.397
I don't know
how to convince you I'm sane

31:37.522 --> 31:39.858
when you've already made up
your mind about me.

31:41.151 --> 31:42.527
I'm here to help you, Sofia.

31:44.070 --> 31:45.697
I have no other agenda
than that.

31:46.906 --> 31:48.074
[gentle music playing]

31:52.245 --> 31:53.830
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door unlocks]

31:59.210 --> 32:01.171
- [door thuds shut, locks]
- [buzzer sounds]

32:01.171 --> 32:04.174
[patients screaming]

32:04.174 --> 32:05.133
[guard] Move!

32:06.885 --> 32:08.219
[suspenseful music playing]

32:30.909 --> 32:33.620
Fuck you, bitch! Bitch! Bitch!

32:33.745 --> 32:34.788
[clanking]

32:35.246 --> 32:37.332
[gasps raggedly] Come here
so I can eat your fucking mouth.

32:37.332 --> 32:39.084
Mouth. Mouth. Mouth.

32:40.960 --> 32:42.962
[gasps softly] Come on, try it.

32:43.088 --> 32:45.757
T-try it. Try it. T-try it.

32:53.223 --> 32:54.766
[eerie musical sting]

32:56.643 --> 32:58.103
You want me to hurt her.

32:58.770 --> 32:59.896
Right?

32:59.896 --> 33:03.233
To what? Prove I'm a killer?
Is that it?

33:03.233 --> 33:06.528
You killed them.
Say it! Say it! Say it!

33:08.947 --> 33:09.948
This is my father.

33:10.073 --> 33:12.826
You're-you're-you're working
for him.

33:12.951 --> 33:14.619
[grunting]

33:20.417 --> 33:21.543
[panting]

33:22.252 --> 33:23.211
End it.

33:24.004 --> 33:25.463
[pleadingly] Please. End it.

33:25.588 --> 33:26.548
End it.

33:27.298 --> 33:28.508
End it.

33:29.968 --> 33:31.553
[cries softly] End it!

33:31.553 --> 33:32.971
- End it! End it!
- [fork stabbing]

33:33.096 --> 33:34.139
[Sofia screams]

33:35.390 --> 33:36.725
[screaming indistinctly]

33:36.725 --> 33:38.560
[Sofia] What happened?

33:40.103 --> 33:41.813
[suspenseful, dramatic music
playing]

33:41.938 --> 33:43.314
What are you doing?

33:43.982 --> 33:45.900
No, no. What is that?

33:45.900 --> 33:47.777
- [clicks]
- It's set.

33:47.777 --> 33:50.321
You can't do this.
I didn't do anything wrong.

33:50.447 --> 33:53.825
This isn't a punishment.
You're agitated, confused.

33:54.451 --> 33:56.036
This'll help you feel
like yourself again.

33:56.036 --> 33:57.704
- [Sofia] Wait.
- [Dr. Ventris] Open wide.

33:57.829 --> 33:58.913
No!

33:58.913 --> 34:00.874
- [Dr. Ventris] Open!
- [muffled screams]

34:01.541 --> 34:03.293
[electricity crackling]

34:03.293 --> 34:04.753
[muffled grunting]

34:04.753 --> 34:06.171
[electricity crackling]

34:08.631 --> 34:10.842
[gagging]

34:11.634 --> 34:14.846
[vomiting and coughing]

34:14.971 --> 34:16.473
[Magpie] Uh-oh.

34:16.473 --> 34:18.308
[coughing]

34:18.308 --> 34:19.351
[Magpie] Hangman?

34:20.518 --> 34:21.603
Are you okay?

34:25.482 --> 34:26.941
[groaning weakly]

34:39.204 --> 34:40.205
[Sofia, softly] What?

34:41.373 --> 34:42.749
[door opens]

34:45.085 --> 34:47.087
[Sofia, weakly]
Why are you doing this?

34:47.212 --> 34:49.589
[panting] I'm innocent.
I'm innocent.

34:49.714 --> 34:53.426
- [electricity crackling]
- [muffled grunting]

34:53.551 --> 34:54.803
[gasps]

34:55.387 --> 34:58.556
[panting]

35:04.020 --> 35:05.188
[breathing shakily]

35:05.188 --> 35:06.815
[whimpers]

35:08.066 --> 35:09.025
[cries]

35:09.025 --> 35:10.318
I didn't kill anyone!

35:11.903 --> 35:13.446
Stop! Stop!

35:13.571 --> 35:15.323
- Please!
- [dial clicking]

35:16.116 --> 35:17.784
[quietly] What if
she's telling the truth?

35:17.909 --> 35:19.285
[Sofia panting]

35:19.411 --> 35:20.954
Careful, Doctor.

35:21.413 --> 35:23.915
- [electricity crackling]
- [muffled grunting]

35:24.040 --> 35:26.251
- [music intensifies]
- [screaming]

35:29.254 --> 35:31.589
- [music swells, ends]
- [screams echoing]

35:31.715 --> 35:33.091
[somber music playing]

35:33.633 --> 35:34.926
[straps tightening]

35:39.931 --> 35:41.975
[music turns menacing]

35:41.975 --> 35:43.226
[dial clicking]

35:43.226 --> 35:45.228
- [electricity crackling]
- [muffled grunting]

35:45.228 --> 35:48.106
[gasping]

35:48.231 --> 35:49.232
[sighs]

35:50.316 --> 35:52.652
[rope creaking]

35:55.238 --> 35:57.240
[eerie music playing]

36:08.418 --> 36:09.711
- Mom?
- [dramatic musical sting]

36:09.711 --> 36:16.134
[gasping]

36:17.260 --> 36:22.515
[panting]

36:22.515 --> 36:24.476
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door opens]

36:25.101 --> 36:26.186
[Julian] Sofia.

36:26.770 --> 36:27.729
You've got a visitor.

36:30.565 --> 36:32.192
- [shackles rattling]
- Go on.

36:34.903 --> 36:35.945
[door clanks]

36:35.945 --> 36:39.115
[divider clattering]

36:39.115 --> 36:40.992
- Alberto.
- Sofia.

36:41.659 --> 36:43.536
[shackles clanking]

36:45.455 --> 36:47.916
- [breathing heavily] Sofia.
- What?

36:47.916 --> 36:50.168
Fuck! I'm so sorry.

36:51.461 --> 36:52.837
You're not going to court.

36:54.005 --> 36:55.465
No one's gonna hear your case.

36:55.465 --> 36:58.301
Your-your doctor, he's claiming
you're unfit to stand trial.

36:58.301 --> 36:59.594
Dr. Rush?

37:00.178 --> 37:01.805
He-he wouldn't do that.

37:01.805 --> 37:05.016
It was the head of Arkham.
Uh, some guy named Ventris.

37:05.725 --> 37:08.436
He wrote the report,
and the judge agreed. It's done.

37:10.313 --> 37:11.189
But that's...

37:12.982 --> 37:13.817
That's not...

37:14.693 --> 37:16.444
I-I did my six months.

37:17.904 --> 37:20.115
- I deserve a trial. I...
- [Alberto sniffles]

37:20.115 --> 37:22.367
I have... rights.

37:22.492 --> 37:23.535
This-this is my life.

37:23.660 --> 37:25.120
We'll file an appeal.

37:25.120 --> 37:27.622
O-or try for a new evaluation.

37:28.206 --> 37:30.667
I don't know. Tell me
what to do, and I'll do it.

37:30.667 --> 37:31.876
- That's it.
- No.

37:33.503 --> 37:35.046
- [quietly] Sofia...
- [chuckles wryly]

37:35.714 --> 37:38.717
Sofia, no, don't. Don't. Please.

37:39.217 --> 37:42.220
I know this is fucked,
but you gotta keep fighting.

37:42.345 --> 37:43.138
[shackles jangle]

37:43.138 --> 37:44.556
I'm not giving up.

37:45.223 --> 37:46.474
[banging]

37:47.225 --> 37:49.769
I swear to God, one day,
I'll get you out of here.

37:51.229 --> 37:52.105
Sofia.

37:54.190 --> 37:55.817
[banging on glass] Sofia!

37:57.736 --> 37:58.903
Sofia!

37:59.070 --> 38:01.322
- [somber music playing]
- [patients chattering]

38:08.538 --> 38:11.499
Sofia. I didn't know Ventris
was gonna write the report.

38:12.083 --> 38:13.293
I tried to stop him.

38:16.254 --> 38:17.088
I'm sorry.

38:18.423 --> 38:19.341
[Magpie] How'd it go?

38:21.593 --> 38:23.845
Uh-oh. Not good?

38:24.888 --> 38:27.974
Well, at least
we can stay friends now.

38:29.059 --> 38:31.519
Best friends. [giggles shrilly]

38:31.519 --> 38:34.564
And I can show the garden.
[giggles]

38:34.564 --> 38:37.233
There aren't any plants, though.
It's more of a yard, really.

38:37.233 --> 38:39.986
I always look for birds,
but I can never see any.

38:40.111 --> 38:41.404
[giggles]

38:41.404 --> 38:43.656
[gasps excitedly] Oh!
He'll give you candy now.

38:44.616 --> 38:45.533
What?

38:46.117 --> 38:48.661
You don't have to lie
to Dr. V anymore.

38:49.496 --> 38:51.247
You can tell him the truth.

38:51.247 --> 38:53.291
He'll give it to you now.
[giggles]

38:53.792 --> 38:55.627
Are you working for him?

38:57.462 --> 38:59.464
Have you been spying on me?

39:00.048 --> 39:00.965
No.

39:01.132 --> 39:03.134
Is that why
he's giving you drugs?

39:03.843 --> 39:05.804
To get information out of me?

39:05.929 --> 39:08.348
[angrily] Don't be silly.
I'm your friend!

39:09.140 --> 39:11.685
[giggles] We're gonna have
so much fun together, too.

39:11.685 --> 39:14.771
We can celebrate holidays
and birthdays.

39:14.771 --> 39:17.440
Mine's in February,
which makes me an Aquarius.

39:17.440 --> 39:19.025
- [grunts]
- [patients gasp]

39:21.319 --> 39:22.987
Wait. Wait!

39:23.113 --> 39:24.698
[Sofia grunting angrily]

39:24.698 --> 39:25.782
[patients screaming]

39:25.782 --> 39:27.409
[screaming angrily]

39:27.409 --> 39:29.494
[thumping wetly]

39:29.619 --> 39:30.662
[grunts angrily]

39:31.162 --> 39:32.580
[ominous music playing]

39:32.580 --> 39:34.499
[patients shrieking]

39:37.627 --> 39:39.921
I told you I'm fucking innocent.

39:47.846 --> 39:48.847
[music ends]

39:52.183 --> 39:53.059
[Julian] Sofia?

39:55.854 --> 39:56.896
Sofia?

39:57.522 --> 39:58.898
[Sofia exhales]

40:02.569 --> 40:03.528
[Sophia breathing]

40:05.530 --> 40:06.531
[Julian exhales]

40:08.074 --> 40:08.950
[sighs]

40:09.576 --> 40:10.910
Thank God you're okay.

40:17.375 --> 40:18.543
I'm glad you called me.

40:20.545 --> 40:23.173
[pants, exhales]

40:23.173 --> 40:24.341
Not too fast.

40:24.341 --> 40:27.886
[panting]

40:28.887 --> 40:30.472
I'm gonna get you
something to eat.

40:31.931 --> 40:33.933
If you wanna get cleaned up,
there's a towel

40:33.933 --> 40:36.394
and a change of clothes
in the guest bath upstairs.

40:42.817 --> 40:44.319
Breakfast is almost ready.

41:01.044 --> 41:02.128
[pills rattling]

41:03.880 --> 41:06.257
[drawer closes]

41:13.390 --> 41:15.225
[breathing heavily]

41:15.225 --> 41:17.477
[footsteps approaching]

41:17.602 --> 41:18.603
[Julian] How you feeling?

41:23.066 --> 41:24.275
Like an idiot.

41:27.404 --> 41:28.363
I trusted him...

41:29.072 --> 41:31.449
when everything in my body
told me not to.

41:33.368 --> 41:35.537
[tuts] I should have killed him
when I had the chance.

41:36.287 --> 41:37.497
Sofia...

41:37.497 --> 41:38.998
I don't even know
where the hell Oz is.

41:38.998 --> 41:41.459
I have no allies, no resources,

41:41.584 --> 41:44.004
and if I'm not on a plane
to Sicily by tomorrow...

41:44.004 --> 41:46.673
[inhales] ...my Uncle Luca...

41:49.467 --> 41:50.635
Well...

41:53.638 --> 41:54.806
Maybe you should go.

41:58.768 --> 42:00.020
Not for your family.

42:00.478 --> 42:01.479
For yourself.

42:02.439 --> 42:04.816
Sofia, you've only been
out of Arkham a few weeks.

42:05.942 --> 42:07.569
You deserve a fresh start,

42:08.194 --> 42:09.571
an opportunity to heal.

42:10.113 --> 42:11.239
Why are you doing this?

42:12.198 --> 42:13.324
What do you want?

42:13.867 --> 42:14.826
To help you.

42:15.368 --> 42:16.286
Mm-hmm.

42:16.870 --> 42:17.996
And to feel better...

42:18.121 --> 42:20.248
or less guilty
for what happened to you.

42:20.248 --> 42:21.624
You quit.

42:22.959 --> 42:23.793
You abandoned me.

42:23.793 --> 42:24.919
I left because I had to,

42:25.503 --> 42:26.504
because I could.

42:27.630 --> 42:29.007
I know
you didn't have that choice,

42:29.132 --> 42:30.050
but I'm here now.

42:32.177 --> 42:33.803
You don't have to pretend
with me.

42:33.803 --> 42:35.472
[tense music playing]

42:35.472 --> 42:37.849
You miss how it was
at Arkham, don't you?

42:39.559 --> 42:40.727
You've had a long night.

42:43.063 --> 42:44.606
The control that you had...

42:45.565 --> 42:46.608
treating me,

42:47.859 --> 42:49.611
rehabilitating me.

42:50.445 --> 42:51.863
I helped Alberto get you out.

42:53.865 --> 42:55.033
And now, here I am...

42:56.534 --> 42:57.952
wearing your clothes.

42:59.162 --> 43:01.456
I haven't forgotten, you know?

43:02.791 --> 43:04.250
The way you looked at me.

43:06.336 --> 43:07.545
So curious.

43:10.215 --> 43:11.549
What did it feel like?

43:12.133 --> 43:15.428
To get to watch
a person unravel?

43:16.721 --> 43:19.265
And now, you're numbing yourself
as punishment.

43:21.267 --> 43:22.394
That's absurd.

43:25.188 --> 43:26.940
My father told me I was sick.

43:29.609 --> 43:30.902
And Dr. Ventris.

43:32.529 --> 43:34.239
And then the doctor after him.

43:35.907 --> 43:37.575
And then the doctor after him.

43:39.911 --> 43:41.746
For ten years,

43:42.872 --> 43:45.667
men have lied to me.

43:47.752 --> 43:48.920
And then I come home,

43:50.088 --> 43:51.256
and it's all the same.

43:54.426 --> 43:55.760
They think I'm broken.

43:57.804 --> 43:58.930
I'm not broken.

44:01.766 --> 44:03.351
I'm not the one who's sick.

44:06.730 --> 44:07.939
And neither are you.

44:11.234 --> 44:12.444
[music fades out]

44:12.444 --> 44:13.778
The world is.

44:15.196 --> 44:17.198
[ominous music playing]

44:23.496 --> 44:24.873
[clicks tongue] You're right.

44:26.041 --> 44:27.500
I deserve a fresh start.

44:29.586 --> 44:31.796
[ominous music continues]

44:31.921 --> 44:34.132
[indistinct chatter
and laughter]

44:34.257 --> 44:35.592
I do want some cheese.

44:35.592 --> 44:37.302
You know what?
I don't want any cheese.

44:37.427 --> 44:38.553
You hold the cheese.

44:39.137 --> 44:41.056
[Viti clearing throat]

44:41.056 --> 44:42.474
[chatter and laughter stop]

44:59.157 --> 45:02.077
[chair dragging loudly]

45:03.828 --> 45:08.583
[chair scooting loudly]

45:16.132 --> 45:17.217
[bottle thuds heavily]

45:18.843 --> 45:23.056
[spoon clinking]

45:23.723 --> 45:25.308
What the hell are you doin'?

45:25.308 --> 45:27.018
Supporting Uncle Luca.

45:27.852 --> 45:29.020
Same as you.

45:29.020 --> 45:30.355
Can you pass the meatballs?

45:33.233 --> 45:34.275
[spoon clangs]

45:36.027 --> 45:37.529
[clinking glass]

45:38.154 --> 45:39.280
[clears throat]

45:40.198 --> 45:43.702
I'd like to express my gratitude
to everyone here.

45:43.827 --> 45:45.870
Tensions are high,

45:45.995 --> 45:49.082
and I wish we was gathered
under different circumstances.

45:49.207 --> 45:52.836
But our Family
has weathered storms before,

45:52.836 --> 45:55.088
and it has only made us
stronger.

45:55.880 --> 45:57.465
- [giggles]
- Gia. Gia.

45:57.465 --> 45:58.717
[Luca] But here, this house,

45:58.842 --> 46:01.886
us, we are
each other's sanctuary,

46:02.012 --> 46:05.724
finding solace and celebration
even in our darkest hour.

46:06.349 --> 46:09.477
My brother used to say
that true strength--

46:09.477 --> 46:11.855
[clinking]

46:13.440 --> 46:15.275
Forgive me. I've never been one
for speeches,

46:15.275 --> 46:16.985
but I did wanna say a few words.

46:17.444 --> 46:20.030
You don't mind,
do you, Uncle Luca?

46:20.030 --> 46:21.072
[Luca grunts]

46:27.746 --> 46:28.621
Wow.

46:30.832 --> 46:32.167
Look at everyone.

46:32.709 --> 46:34.419
I believe the last time
we were all together

46:34.544 --> 46:37.464
was my father's birthday
10 years ago.

46:38.089 --> 46:39.924
I'm sure
you all remember that night.

46:42.385 --> 46:43.636
I know I do.

46:43.762 --> 46:45.347
Come on. It's time for bed.

46:45.347 --> 46:47.265
But Daddy said there'd be cake.

46:47.390 --> 46:48.600
[Sofia] Take a seat, Carla.

46:54.647 --> 46:56.775
Gia, go get ready for bed, okay?

47:02.030 --> 47:03.114
As you all know,

47:05.408 --> 47:07.952
I was stuffed
in Arkham State Hospital

47:08.078 --> 47:09.371
for a decade...

47:09.371 --> 47:10.580
[clears throat]

47:10.580 --> 47:14.209
...convicted
of murdering seven women.

47:15.919 --> 47:17.128
Summer Gleeson,

47:17.796 --> 47:19.297
Taylor Montgomery,

47:19.422 --> 47:21.132
Yolanda Jones,

47:21.257 --> 47:22.676
Nancy Hoffman,

47:22.676 --> 47:24.302
Susanna Weakley,

47:24.928 --> 47:26.513
Devri Blake,

47:26.638 --> 47:28.139
and Tricia Becker.

47:29.140 --> 47:30.809
Their names are worth saying.

47:32.602 --> 47:34.771
Victims are
so quickly forgotten,

47:34.771 --> 47:36.231
aren't they?

47:36.815 --> 47:40.068
Our stories are... rarely told.

47:40.068 --> 47:42.862
Okay, all right,
I think that's--

47:45.031 --> 47:45.907
Yes?

47:46.491 --> 47:47.450
Hmm?

47:51.204 --> 47:53.331
I've had a lot of time
to reflect.

47:55.166 --> 47:56.501
And I have to say...

47:58.795 --> 48:00.880
I was genuinely surprised

48:01.631 --> 48:04.384
at how many of you wrote letters

48:04.384 --> 48:06.720
telling the judge
that I was mentally ill,

48:07.220 --> 48:08.596
like my mother.

48:09.264 --> 48:11.349
Not that the judge
needed much convincing.

48:11.474 --> 48:13.059
My father saw to that.

48:13.560 --> 48:16.271
Still, I trusted you.

48:19.941 --> 48:21.067
I loved you.

48:23.403 --> 48:27.198
And yet, not one of you...
[inhales shakily]

48:27.323 --> 48:29.868
...tried to help me.

48:31.703 --> 48:33.538
Except for my brother,

48:34.372 --> 48:37.042
the man you all flew in
to mourn.

48:38.251 --> 48:42.047
And you know,
the real thorn in my side

48:42.172 --> 48:44.716
is that, unlike everyone here...

48:46.718 --> 48:48.261
I was innocent.

48:49.054 --> 48:51.056
I mean... [laughs]

48:52.015 --> 48:54.559
Jesus Christ, Milos has
a higher body count than I do.

48:54.684 --> 48:55.977
[thuds] Sofia!

49:00.523 --> 49:03.068
I know you're all anxious
for me to leave.

49:04.361 --> 49:05.653
[chuckles]

49:05.653 --> 49:07.614
No one has been shy about that.

49:11.409 --> 49:13.703
I'd really hoped
that it would be different.

49:15.080 --> 49:16.498
But I understand.

49:20.251 --> 49:22.587
I don't fit
into this family anymore.

49:24.422 --> 49:26.841
So, tomorrow,
I'm starting a new life.

49:27.842 --> 49:29.010
For the first time,

49:29.761 --> 49:30.970
I have hope.

49:35.934 --> 49:38.103
To new beginnings.

49:38.937 --> 49:40.146
[tense music playing]

49:40.146 --> 49:41.189
Cent'anni.

49:43.274 --> 49:44.859
[tense music continues]

50:19.853 --> 50:21.479
[music turns menacing]

50:34.826 --> 50:36.953
[menacing ethereal music
playing]

50:36.953 --> 50:38.913
[Sofia] Are you ready
for some cake?

50:40.248 --> 50:42.667
I have a corner piece
with your name on it.

50:42.792 --> 50:44.210
It's extra chocolatey,

50:44.210 --> 50:46.504
with tons of frosting.

50:48.340 --> 50:49.215
But...

50:50.300 --> 50:52.344
we have to eat it
in the greenhouse.

50:52.469 --> 50:53.678
Should we tell my mom?

50:53.803 --> 50:56.014
[shushing] No.
We don't need to wake her up.

50:57.057 --> 50:59.267
It can be our little secret, okay?

51:01.811 --> 51:02.771
[cutlery clinking]

51:02.771 --> 51:04.314
[Sofia] Would you like
some more?

51:04.314 --> 51:06.024
I should go to bed.

51:09.069 --> 51:13.782
You know, my brother and I
used to sleep out here

51:14.366 --> 51:15.575
when we were little.

51:16.993 --> 51:19.954
We would snuggle up in blankets,

51:19.954 --> 51:23.541
and we would pretend
that this was a jungle.

51:26.378 --> 51:28.213
Should we sleep
out here tonight?

51:28.797 --> 51:30.298
That could be fun, right?

51:35.512 --> 51:38.139
My mom told me
not to talk to you.

51:38.139 --> 51:40.475
She said you did bad things.

51:41.434 --> 51:42.644
She's right.

51:44.396 --> 51:46.398
I did do bad things.

51:47.065 --> 51:47.982
Why?

51:49.234 --> 51:52.987
Well, my father locked me away
in a dungeon

51:52.987 --> 51:56.616
with a bunch of scary monsters,
and... [inhales]

51:56.616 --> 51:59.911
...I had to fight them
to survive.

52:03.206 --> 52:04.916
Am I gonna get locked away?

52:05.041 --> 52:07.919
No, no, no. You don't have
to worry about that.

52:09.254 --> 52:10.338
I'm gonna make sure

52:10.880 --> 52:13.258
that you never have
to fight any monsters.

52:13.800 --> 52:14.968
Okay?

52:16.886 --> 52:18.263
Now, get some sleep.

52:33.111 --> 52:35.321
[birds chirping]

52:35.321 --> 52:36.364
[ethereal music ends]

52:41.453 --> 52:42.620
[Gia stirs]

52:43.538 --> 52:44.998
[quietly] Go back to sleep.

52:45.582 --> 52:46.958
I'll be right back.

53:01.139 --> 53:03.475
["So Long, My Love"
by Sarah Vaughan playing]

53:12.650 --> 53:16.738
♪ So long, my love ♪

53:16.738 --> 53:19.657
♪ Goodbye, farewell ♪

53:19.657 --> 53:24.204
♪ Adieu ♪

53:25.455 --> 53:28.375
♪ So long, my love ♪

53:28.500 --> 53:29.459
[gas hissing]

53:29.584 --> 53:34.339
♪ It's obviously through ♪

53:36.132 --> 53:39.969
♪ Let's make the final scene ♪

53:39.969 --> 53:41.012
[hissing stops]

53:41.137 --> 53:43.765
♪ Nice and clean ♪

53:43.765 --> 53:49.187
♪ No aftermath ♪

53:49.187 --> 53:54.234
♪ Omit the bitter talk ♪

53:54.234 --> 54:01.199
♪ And just walk us
a separate path ♪

54:02.283 --> 54:04.035
♪ Face it ♪

54:05.245 --> 54:08.498
♪ The shortest kiss ♪

54:08.498 --> 54:15.547
♪ Is now an endless thing ♪

54:18.049 --> 54:21.386
♪ I seem to miss ♪

54:21.386 --> 54:28.435
♪ The bells that used to ring ♪

54:28.935 --> 54:33.231
♪ So like they say in France ♪

54:33.231 --> 54:40.280
♪ When romance is all fini ♪

54:41.906 --> 54:47.412
♪ Please give me my chapeau ♪

54:47.412 --> 54:54.461
♪ I've got to get goin' ♪

54:56.504 --> 55:00.133
♪ I'll say so long, my love ♪

55:04.554 --> 55:07.098
♪ Be strong, my love ♪

55:10.602 --> 55:15.273
♪ So long, my love ♪

55:15.398 --> 55:21.780
♪ Before you say it to me ♪

55:21.905 --> 55:23.031
[tapping]

55:25.784 --> 55:28.203
♪ So long, goodbye ♪

55:28.203 --> 55:29.704
Put your pants on, Johnny.

55:31.122 --> 55:32.332
We need to talk.

55:35.293 --> 55:36.169
[song ends]

55:39.506 --> 55:41.883
["Strange Little Girl"
by the Stranglers playing]

55:43.802 --> 55:45.136
♪ One day you'll see ♪

55:45.261 --> 55:47.972
♪ A strange little girl
look at you ♪

55:51.434 --> 55:52.727
♪ One day you'll see ♪

55:52.727 --> 55:55.438
♪ A strange little girl
feeling blue ♪

55:58.817 --> 56:01.820
♪ She'd run to the town
one day ♪

56:01.945 --> 56:04.823
♪ Leaving home
and the country fair ♪

56:05.532 --> 56:07.242
♪ Just beware ♪

56:09.327 --> 56:10.995
♪ When you're there ♪

56:12.664 --> 56:14.499
♪ Strange little girl ♪

56:17.794 --> 56:21.881
♪ She didn't know how to live
in a town that was rough ♪

56:25.552 --> 56:26.803
♪ It didn't take long ♪

56:26.803 --> 56:29.597
♪ Before she knew
she'd had enough ♪

56:32.976 --> 56:36.021
♪ Walking home
in her wrapped up world ♪

56:36.146 --> 56:39.065
♪ She survived,
but she's feeling old ♪

56:39.816 --> 56:41.693
♪ 'Cause she found ♪

56:43.695 --> 56:45.697
♪ All things cold ♪

56:47.949 --> 56:50.952
♪ Strange little girl,
where are you going? ♪

56:51.786 --> 56:54.789
♪ Strange little girl,
where are you going? ♪

56:55.582 --> 56:59.461
♪ Do you know
where you could be going? ♪

57:00.295 --> 57:03.340
♪ Strange little girl,
where are you going? ♪

57:04.341 --> 57:07.927
♪ Do you know
where you could be going? ♪

57:08.678 --> 57:09.554
[song ends]

57:09.763 --> 57:12.223
[suspenseful,
dramatic music playing]

58:01.648 --> 58:03.608
[music ends]
